% Synthesize a Boolean program from input/output examples.
% Query: synthesize(P),zero(A),one(B),evaluate(P,A,B),evaluate(P,B,A)
% All choices are explicit; identity, negate, constant, zero and one are
% ordinary relations whose meaning is supplied by these rules.
synthesize(P) <=> (identity(P);negate(P);constant(P,C),(zero(C);one(C))).
identity(P) \ evaluate(P,X,Y) <=> X=Y.
negate(P), zero(X) \ evaluate(P,X,Y) <=> one(Y).
negate(P), one(X) \ evaluate(P,X,Y) <=> zero(Y).
constant(P,C) \ evaluate(P,X,Y) <=> C=Y.
zero(X), one(X) <=> fail.
